      {
        "content": "Given:\n- Total crayons: 48\n- Kiley takes 1/4 of them away\n- Joe takes away half of the remaining crayons\n\nStep 1: Calculate how many crayons Kiley takes.\n\\[ \\text{Crayons Kiley takes} = \\frac{1}{4} \\times 48 = 12 \\]\nStep 2: Calculate the remaining crayons after Kiley takes her share.\n\\[ \\text{Remaining crayons} = 48 - 12 = 36 \\]\nStep 3: Calculate how many crayons Joe takes.\n\\[ \\text{Crayons Joe takes} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 36 = 18 \\]\nStep 4: Calculate the remaining crayons after Joe takes his share.\n\\[ \\text{Remaining crayons} = 36 - 18 = 18 \\]\n\nThe exact number of crayons left is 18.\n\nFINAL: 18",
